WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.015
Google Cloud CLI commands run within a
selected account, project,

2
00:00:05.095 --> 00:00:08.884
configuration, region, zone, and
credential context.

3
00:00:08.964 --> 00:00:13.398
In automation, those values may come from
named configurations,

4
00:00:13.478 --> 00:00:17.750
environment variables, CI/CD variables,
active local state,

5
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.829
service accounts, federated credentials,
or metadata-based identity.

6
00:00:22.909 --> 00:00:28.391
A secure script should not assume that the
currently selected project, account,

7
00:00:28.471 --> 00:00:32.663
or default region is correct just because
a command would run.

8
00:00:32.743 --> 00:00:36.693
Target validation should happen before
meaningful work.

9
00:00:36.773 --> 00:00:41.691
A script should confirm the expected
project ID, active configuration,

10
00:00:41.771 --> 00:00:44.754
account, region, zone, environment label,

11
00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:48.704
and target resource identifiers before
making changes.

12
00:00:48.784 --> 00:00:51.686
It should also keep organization, folder,

13
00:00:51.766 --> 00:00:55.313
and project boundaries in mind at a
defensive level,

14
00:00:55.393 --> 00:01:00.311
because those boundaries shape policy
inheritance, IAM expectations,

15
00:01:00.391 --> 00:01:01.600
and blast radius.

16
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.759
Development, staging, and production
should have separate assumptions,

17
00:01:06.839 --> 00:01:11.031
credentials, approval paths, and
monitoring expectations.

18
00:01:11.111 --> 00:01:14.658
A development helper may prioritize fast
feedback,

19
00:01:14.738 --> 00:01:18.850
while a production workflow may require a
protected branch,

20
00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:24.896
release ticket, deployment window,
operator confirmation, or environment approval.

21
00:01:24.976 --> 00:01:30.861
The script should reflect those
differences instead of relying on naming conventions

22
00:01:30.941 --> 00:01:31.425
alone.

23
00:01:31.505 --> 00:01:36.342
Environment variables and CI/CD variables
should be treated as input.

24
00:01:36.422 --> 00:01:42.065
They can be stale, missing, inherited, or
inconsistent with the requested action.

25
00:01:42.145 --> 00:01:45.934
If the project, account, configuration,
region, zone,

26
00:01:46.014 --> 00:01:51.738
or resource target cannot be confirmed,
the script should stop with a clear message.

27
00:01:51.818 --> 00:01:57.300
The safest wrong-target change is one that
fails before it reaches Google Cloud.
